ACMsg.STM32_HT16K33SEGMENT14_HT16K33SEGMENT14_SET_GLYPH = "Puts the input character matrix (a 16-bit integer) into the specified row, adding a decimal point if required. Character matrix value is calculated by setting the bit(s) representing the segment(s) you want illuminated: 0                           9 _ 5 |   | 1           8 \\ | / 10 |   |                        \\|/ 6  - -  7 4 |   | 2              /|              | _ |                   13 / | \\ 11          . 14 3                           12 Bit 14 is the period, but this is set with parameter 3 Nb. Bit 15 is not read by the display Paramètres : glyph (int):   The glyph pattern. digit (int):   The digit to show the glyph. Default: 0 (leftmost digit). Retour : The instance (self)";
ACMsg.STM32_HT16K33SEGMENT14_HT16K33SEGMENT14_SET_NUMBER = "Present single decimal value (0-9) at the specified digit. This method updates the display buffer, but does not send the buffer to the display itself. Call 'update()' to render the buffer on the display. Paramètres : number (int):  The number to show. digit (int):   The digit to show the number. Default: 0 (leftmost digit). Retour : The instance (self)";
